{hr}← {opts}BarChart2 values
  ; ev; fn; labels; missing; parms; print; size; title; type; wait; xl; yl
  ; Here; HtmlHdr; HtmlDraw; JScript; PrintPdf
  ; ⎕IO
⍝ Draw a bar chart using Chart.js via HtmlRenderer.
⍝ Warning: requires Internet access when called.
⍝ Terminates on window close or Escape when wait=1.
⍝   options:
⍝     An optional namespace containing several variables:
⍝       var     description                       default
⍝       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
⍝       values  the values, overriding those      ,values
⍝               presented
⍝       type    type of chart.                    'bar'
⍝       title   the bar chart title               'My Title'
⍝       xl      the x-axis label                  'ITEMS'
⍝       yl      the y-axis label                  'VALUES'
⍝       labels  a vector containing the          '1' '2' '3' ... ≢values
⍝               label for each bar chart item
⍝       size    Size of the window                40 40
⍝       print   Print the chart as a pdf          ''
⍝               with name <print>.pdf.
⍝               Ignored if '' (default).
⍝       wait    wait for close/Escape before      0
⍝               returning
⍝  values:
⍝       A vector of real numbers, one per bar chart item.
⍝       See also the values option.

⎕IO← 0
:If 900⌶0
      opts← ()
:EndIf

values type title xl yl labels size print wait← opts ⎕VGET(
      'values'   (,values)
      'type'     'bar' 
      'title'    'My Chart'
      'xl'       'ITEMS'
      'yl'       'VALUES'
      'labels'   ⎕NULL                              ⍝ Null: Undefined, we'll set it below
      'size'     (40 40)
      'print'    ''                                 ⍝ If empty, nothing is printed.
      'wait'     0
)
⍝  Set labels
:If ⎕NULL≡labels
      labels← ⍕¨1+⍳≢values                          ⍝ Values '1' '3' etc.
:ElseIf labels>⍥≢values
      11 ⎕SIGNAL⍨'Too many labels'
:ElseIf 3 5 11∊⍨80|⎕DR labels                       ⍝ Numeric labels
      labels← ⍕¨labels
:EndIf
⍝ If too few labels, the rest are padded with ⊂'' (a null string)
 ⋄ missing← ⊂''
labels,← missing⍴⍨values-⍥≢labels

⍝ :Section Support Functions 
      Here← { ('^\h*⍝', ⍵, ' (.*)')⎕S'\1'⎕NR 1⊃⎕XSI} ⍝ ⍵: a prefix (e.g. 'H')
      PrintPdf← { 
          11:: _← 0⊣ ⎕← 'DOMAIN ERROR: Invalid filename: ',⍵
            WL← 0.1∘{ ⍵≤0: 0 ⋄ hr.IsLoading: _← ⍺ ∇ ⍵- ⎕DL ⍺ ⋄ 1 } 
            cL cR← 'Chart did not load. ' 'Created '
            uP← cL, 'Unable to print ',⍵
          ~WL 30: _← 1⊣ ⎕← cL, ⍵
          hr.PrintToPDF ⍵⊣ ⎕DL 2: _← 1⊣ ⎕← cR, ⍵  
          1: _← 0⊣ ⎕← uP 
      }
⍝ :EndSection Support Functions 

      HCode← { case data← ⊆⍵ ⋄  Case← case∘{⍺ ≡⍥⊃⍵}
    Case 'Hdr':   '__SRC__' ⎕R chartSrc⊣ Here 'H'
    Case 'Def':   ⎕TC[1],¨ '__TYPE__' ⎕R data⊢ Here'D'
    Case 'Exec':  '__PARMS__' ⎕R data⊢ Here 'E'  
      
   ⍝H  <!DOCTYPE html>
   ⍝H  <html>
   ⍝H   <head>
   ⍝H     <script src="__SRC__"></script>
   ⍝H     <style>
   ⍝H       html,body{height:100%;margin:0 ;}
   ⍝H       #chart{width:98vw;height:100vh;}
   ⍝H     </style>
   ⍝H   </head>
   ⍝H   <body><div id="chart"></div>
   ⍝-------------------
   ⍝D <script>
   ⍝D /**
   ⍝D  * DrawChart(spec, containerId)
   ⍝D  *   spec.labels : array of category names (x axis)
   ⍝D  *   spec.values : array of numbers (bar heights)
   ⍝D  *   spec.xLabel : legend for the x axis
   ⍝D  *   spec.yLabel : legend for the y axis
   ⍝D  *   spec.title  : chart title
   ⍝D  */
   ⍝D function DrawChart(spec, containerId) {
   ⍝D   const host = document.getElementById(containerId);
   ⍝D   host.innerHTML = "<canvas></canvas>";
   ⍝D   new Chart(host.querySelector("canvas"), {
   ⍝D     type: "__TYPE__",
   ⍝D     data: {
   ⍝D       labels: spec.labels,
   ⍝D       datasets: [{
   ⍝D         data: spec.values,
   ⍝D         backgroundColor: "#4682b4",
   ⍝D         borderColor: "#2f5b7a",
   ⍝D         borderWidth: 1
   ⍝D       }]
   ⍝D     },
   ⍝D     options: {
   ⍝D       responsive: true,
   ⍝D       maintainAspectRatio: false,
   ⍝D       layout: {
   ⍝D           padding: {         // Spacing in pixels
   ⍝D             left: 10,
   ⍝D             right: 10,
   ⍝D             top: 5,
   ⍝D             bottom: 5
   ⍝D           }
   ⍝D       },
   ⍝D       plugins: {
   ⍝D         legend: { display: false },
   ⍝D         title: {
   ⍝D           display: !!spec.title,
   ⍝D           text: spec.title || "",
   ⍝D           font: { size: 25, weight: "bold" }
   ⍝D         },
   ⍝D         tooltip: {
   ⍝D           callbacks: { label: ctx => `${ctx.parsed.y}` }
   ⍝D         }
   ⍝D       },
   ⍝D       scales: {
   ⍝D         x: {
   ⍝D           title: { display: !!spec.xLabel, text: spec.xLabel || "",
   ⍝D                    font: { size: 14, weight: "bold" } }
   ⍝D         },
   ⍝D         y: {
   ⍝D           beginAtZero: true,
   ⍝D           title: { display: !!spec.yLabel, text: spec.yLabel || "",
   ⍝D                    font: { size: 14, weight: "bold" } }
   ⍝D         }
   ⍝D       }
   ⍝D     }
   ⍝D   });
   ⍝D }
   ⍝D </script>
   ⍝-------------------
   ⍝E       <script>DrawChart(__PARMS__,"chart");</script>
   ⍝E     </body>
   ⍝E   </html>
}

chartSrc←  'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.7/dist/chart.umd.min.js'
parms← ⎕JSON (
      title: title
      xLabel: xl
      yLabel: yl
      labels: ,⊆labels
      values: values
)
⍝  Start up the Renderer
'hr'⎕WC'HTMLRenderer' 
hr.HTML← ∊( 
      HCode 'Hdr' chartSrc 
      HCode 'Def' type 
      HCode 'Exec' parms 
)
hr.(Size Caption)← (2⍴size)title

⍝  Terminating...
:If ×≢print      
      PrintPdf print,'.pdf'
:EndIf 
:If wait
      hr← ⎕DQ'hr'
:EndIf
